WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.140
MAID Hansard record.

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:04.909
What MPs said when they voted to kill.

00:00:04.909 --> 00:00:15.863
This page presents the parliamentary record of Canada's MAID debates — the actual words MPs used during Bill C-14 in 2016 and Bill C-7 in 2021.

00:00:15.863 --> 00:00:18.954
These are not opinions or interpretations.

00:00:18.954 --> 00:00:23.988
They are direct citations from Hansard, the official record of parliamentary proceedings.

00:00:23.988 --> 00:00:27.443
Every quote is sourced to its specific Hansard entry.

00:00:27.443 --> 00:00:32.307
Bill C-14 passed 186 to 137.

00:00:32.307 --> 00:00:36.092
Bill C-7 expanded MAID to non-terminal conditions.

00:00:36.092 --> 00:00:39.511
The MPs who voted for these bills spoke on the record.

00:00:39.511 --> 00:00:41.624
Their words are preserved.

00:00:41.624 --> 00:00:43.704
They cannot be erased.

00:00:43.704 --> 00:00:52.727
And they reveal that the expansion to non-terminal conditions — including PTSD soldiers and spinal cord injuries — was explicitly contemplated from the very beginning.

00:00:52.727 --> 00:00:54.943
The record they can't erase.

00:00:54.943 --> 00:01:00.636
Every MP who voted for Bill C-14 and Bill C-7 is on the Hansard record.

00:01:00.636 --> 00:01:02.284
Their names.

00:01:02.284 --> 00:01:03.852
Their words.

00:01:03.852 --> 00:01:05.374
Their votes.

00:01:05.374 --> 00:01:12.045
The Minister of Justice explicitly named PTSD soldiers as potential MAID candidates in 2016.

00:01:12.045 --> 00:01:19.022
The expansion to non-terminal conditions was discussed during C-14 — five years before C-7 made it law.

00:01:19.022 --> 00:01:21.829
Disability organizations warned them.

00:01:21.829 --> 00:01:23.772
The UN warned them.

00:01:23.772 --> 00:01:25.590
They voted yes.

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:29.715
Seventy-six thousand four hundred and seventy-five people are dead.

00:01:29.715 --> 00:01:32.738
The parliamentary record preserves what they said.

00:01:32.738 --> 00:01:35.545
TENET5 ensures it is not forgotten.
